From 352332af4b61d074e67d18364348df6ca0cf4c1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 19:13:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03695/11362] [outer-loop][prototype] Tier-schedule graft +
 A/B: NULL (candidate ordering is not just-explore's edge)

Grafted just-explore's verbatim 5-tier salience schedule (T0 salient+medium-width first ... T4 status-bar)
into rich_action_candidates behind CARNOT_ARC_TIER_SCHEDULE=1 (default off = byte-identical flat path;
smoke confirms it front-loads a salient button over a big dull blob). A/B vs the flat area*rarity sort on
the 5 head-to-head win-games + 7 regression games: tier NEVER beats flat (budget 1000 AND 4000), zero
regression. VERDICT TIER_NULL_no_win. Fair-budget (4000) retest decomposes the h2h gap: ft09/r11l solve
with the FLAT order at 4x budget (they were the offline replay-overhead budget artifact, not schedule;
the LIVE agent is stateful so doesn't share it); bp35/m0r0 stay 0 even at 4x = a REAL gap the tier
schedule does NOT close (just-explore's edge there is a deeper frontier/navigation mechanism). Graft is
parity-safe; NOT merged (null). Branch only.
